course: dictionary
lesson: 404
title: Two meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and appendix is one of them. You can tell which meaning is meant by reading the words around it. This is context again. In a science or health text, appendix means a small part of your body. In a book or report, it means an extra section at the end.
explain: Look at this example: «Keyhole surgery uses small cuts and a camera, so healing is usually quicker and scars smaller; appendix operations are often done this way.» Surgery, healing and scars are clues that the body meaning is the right one. The sentence is about a doctor's operation, not about pages.
explain: Ask yourself: what is the topic? If the text is about the body, the clues will point to an organ. If it is about a book, the clues will be pages, tables, maps or data. Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: The appendix is a small, tube-shaped organ attached to the large intestine, on the lower right side of your tummy.
fact: When the appendix swells and hurts, this is called appendicitis, and it needs a doctor quickly.
fact: Appendicitis is often treated with an operation, and keyhole surgery uses small cuts and a camera.
fact: An appendix in a book or report is an extra section at the end with more information, such as tables, maps or data.
fact: The plural of appendix is «appendices», which is often used for books, or «appendixes».
exercise: «Keyhole surgery uses small cuts and a camera.» What does keyhole surgery use? | *Small cuts and a camera | Big cuts and a microscope | A map and a table | Loud music and a whistle
exercise: «The report has an appendix with tables of data at the back.» What is the appendix in this sentence? | *An extra section at the end with more information | A kind of pain in your leg | A tube for a drink | A small organ inside your tummy
exercise: Sam's doctor said his appendix was swollen and sore. What does appendix mean here? | An extra section at the end of a book | *A small organ inside the tummy | A map of the town | A type of bird
test: Look at this sentence: «The table of results is in the appendix.» Is appendix about a book or the body? | A kind of bird | The body | *A book or report | A school bell
test: What is appendicitis? | *When the appendix swells and hurts | When you eat too fast | When you have a cold | When a book has no pages
exam: In «appendix operations are often done this way», which word is the clue that shows the body meaning? | Way | Often | *Operations | Appendix
